IMPORT prelude

-- Common Services Tunnels Act 2018 (Singapore) -- what the Act asks of owners and occupiers of land in a common services
-- tunnel (CST) area, of anyone carrying out engineering works there, and of utility suppliers: entry on notice (s 9),
-- obstruction of ancillary structures (s 10), upkeep (s 11), engineering works in a protection zone (s 12), laying utility
-- infrastructure on public land (s 13), the penalties (ss 10 to 15), liability of officers (s 16(2)), composition (s 19),
-- appeal to the Minister (s 20) and when service by post takes effect (s 22(5)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation
-- on 31 December 2021", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CSTA2018.txt (SSO current version as at 1 October
-- 2026). The only amendment annotated in the body is [40/2019] on s 18 (injunctions; Supreme Court of Judicature (Amendment)
-- Act 2019, in force 2 January 2021 per the Legislative History).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0092 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. SCOPED to the duties and offences that land on a private owner, occupier, builder or utility
-- supplier. Not encoded: appointment of CST Authorities and authorised officers (ss 4, 5), declaring and changing CST areas
-- (ss 6 to 8), the definitions of utility service and ancillary facility beyond their use here, s 15 information notices
-- beyond the penalty, unincorporated associations (s 17), injunctions (s 18), service methods other than the timing rule,
-- protection from liability (s 23), exemptions (s 24) and regulations (s 25, except the cap on a regulations offence). No
-- regulations were retrieved, so which offences are compoundable, and where any protection zone lies, are unknown here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the finished naive rows (the
-- writing-l4-rules skill was not available to load). No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Common Services Tunnels Act 2018 -- land and works`

§§ `9 -- entry on land in a CST area`

-- s 9(2): an authorised person "must not enter any land that is occupied without giving the owner or occupier of the land at
-- least 7 days' notice of intention to do so unless -- (a) the authorised person is of the opinion that an emergency exists
-- which necessitates immediate entry; or (b) the entry is required only for the purpose of an inspection or a survey."
-- s 9(3)(b): notice is deemed given if affixed to a conspicuous part of the land. s 9(6): no fee, charge or expense is payable
-- to the owner or occupier of private land on account of the entry.
GIVEN `the land is occupied` IS A BOOLEAN, `an emergency in the officer's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN, `inspection or survey only` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `notice of entry is required` IF
    `the land is occupied` AND (NOT `an emergency in the officer's opinion`) AND (NOT `inspection or survey only`)

GIVEN `occupied` IS A BOOLEAN, `emergency` IS A BOOLEAN, `inspection only` IS A BOOLEAN, `days of notice given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entry satisfies the notice rule` IF
    (NOT `notice of entry is required` `occupied` `emergency` `inspection only`) OR `days of notice given` AT LEAST 7

§§ `10 -- obstructing an ancillary structure`

-- s 10(1): "A person must not, without the written approval of an authorised officer -- (a) erect or place any structure or
-- object across or within any ancillary structure of a common services tunnel that is within a common services tunnel area;
-- or (b) obstruct or cause an obstruction to any ancillary structure". (5): contravening (1), or a specified person failing to
-- comply with a removal order under (2), is an offence. (7): "person" does not include the Government, a public authority or
-- a person acting on their behalf. An ancillary structure includes an entrance or exit, which includes a manhole (s 2(1)).
GIVEN `placed or obstructed` IS A BOOLEAN, `had written approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed to comply with a removal order` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acts for the Government or a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the obstruction is an offence` IF
        (NOT `acts for the Government or a public authority`)
    AND (    (`placed or obstructed` AND (NOT `had written approval`))
          OR `failed to comply with a removal order`)

-- s 10(3): the officer may remove it "(a) if the specified person fails to comply with the order ...; or (b) if access to or
-- through the ancillary structure ... is required immediately." (4): the cost is recoverable "(a) where ... removed under
-- subsection (3)(a), from the specified person to whom the order ... was served; or (b) where ... removed under subsection
-- (3)(b), from the owner or occupier of the land from which the structure, object or obstruction was removed."
DECLARE RemovalGround IS ONE OF
    `the order was not complied with`
    `access was needed immediately`

DECLARE Payer IS ONE OF
    `the person served with the order`
    `the owner or occupier of the land`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A RemovalGround
GIVETH A Payer
DECIDE `who pays for removal` IS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `the order was not complied with` THEN `the person served with the order`
    WHEN `access was needed immediately` THEN `the owner or occupier of the land`

§§ `11 -- upkeep of an ancillary structure`

-- s 11(1): an owner or occupier of land in a CST area on which an ancillary structure is located "must take reasonable measures
-- to keep and maintain the ancillary structure ... in good and serviceable repair." (3): the cost of works ordered under (2)
-- "must be borne by the owner or occupier of the land on whom the order is served." (4): "without reasonable excuse"
-- contravening (1) or failing to comply with an order is an offence. (7): owner or occupier excludes the Government or a public
-- authority.
GIVEN `failed to keep in repair or to comply with an order` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is the Government or a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner commits the upkeep offence` IF
    `failed to keep in repair or to comply with an order` AND (NOT `has a reasonable excuse`) AND (NOT `is the Government or a public authority`)

§§ `12 -- engineering works in a CST protection zone`

-- s 12(1): "A person must not, without the prior written approval of an authorised officer, carry out any engineering works
-- within a common services tunnel protection zone." (8): contravening (1) or any condition of approval is an offence. (9):
-- "engineering works" means "any kind of construction work that may affect the structural integrity of a common services
-- tunnel ... and includes -- (a) building works ...; (b) any act of excavating ... in connection with ... renovation ...
-- (iii) any soil investigation work; (c) any act of boring, dredging, jacking, levelling, piling or tunnelling ...; (d) the
-- driving or sinking of any earth rod ...; and (e) any storage or placement of large construction equipment, construction
-- materials and stockpiling of earth or heavy objects". (10): the Government and public authorities are excluded.
-- Parking a private car is not named and is not construction work: that it falls outside is an INFERENCE.
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `building works`
    `excavating for a renovation`
    `soil investigation`
    `piling`
    `stockpiling earth`
    `parking a private car`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is engineering works` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `parking a private car` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the works` IS AN Activity, `within a protection zone` IS A BOOLEAN, `had prior written approval` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `breached a condition` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a public body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the works are an offence` IF
    `the activity is engineering works` `the works` AND `within a protection zone`
    AND ((NOT `had prior written approval`) OR `breached a condition`)
    AND (NOT `is a public body`)

§§ `13 -- laying utility infrastructure on public land`

-- s 13(1): "a supplier of utility services must not lay, place or install ... on, under or over any public land within a
-- common services tunnel area any utility services infrastructure without the written approval of an authorised officer."
-- (4): the officer may make it a condition precedent that the supplier "execute an agreement for the use of the common
-- services tunnel". (5): contravening (1) or breaching a condition is an offence. (6): the Government and public authorities
-- are not suppliers for this section. The prohibition is confined to PUBLIC land; s 12 still applies elsewhere.
GIVEN `on public land` IS A BOOLEAN, `within a CST area` IS A BOOLEAN, `had approval to lay` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `breached a condition of approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `the supplier is a public body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the laying is an offence` IF
    `on public land` AND `within a CST area`
    AND ((NOT `had approval to lay`) OR `breached a condition of approval`)
    AND (NOT `the supplier is a public body`)

§§ `10 to 15, 25(3) -- penalties`

-- ss 10(5), 11(4), 12(8), 13(5): "a fine not exceeding $20,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- exceeding $1,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction." s 14 (obstructing an
-- officer): "a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both." s 15(3), (4)
-- (failing to answer an information notice; a false or misleading answer): $10,000. s 25(3)(b): regulations may create
-- offences punishable with a fine not exceeding $5,000 or 6 months or both.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `an obstruction offence`
    `an upkeep offence`
    `an engineering works offence`
    `a utility laying offence`
    `obstructing an officer`
    `failing to answer an information notice`
    `giving a false answer`
    `a regulations offence`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the base fine` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to answer an information notice` THEN 10000
    WHEN `giving a false answer` THEN 10000
    WHEN `a regulations offence` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 20000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the daily fine` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an obstruction offence` THEN 1000
    WHEN `an upkeep offence` THEN 1000
    WHEN `an engineering works offence` THEN 1000
    WHEN `a utility laying offence` THEN 1000
    OTHERWISE 0

-- Days are counted as whole days; "or part of a day" means a part day counts as a day. The caller rounds up.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine` IS
    `the base fine` `the offence` PLUS (`the daily fine` `the offence` TIMES `days continuing after conviction`)

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 6
    WHEN `a regulations offence` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `16(2) -- officers of a corporation`

-- s 16(2): where a corporation commits an offence, an officer (or an individual involved in management "in a position to
-- influence the conduct of the corporation") who "(i) consented or connived, or conspired with others ...; (ii) is ...
-- knowingly concerned in, or is party to, the commission of the offence ...; or (iii) knew or ought reasonably to have known
-- that the offence ... would be or is being committed, and failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent or stop" it "shall
-- be guilty of that same offence". (5): whether or not the corporation is convicted.
GIVEN `is an officer or influential manager` IS A BOOLEAN, `consented, connived or conspired` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knowingly concerned` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or ought to have known and took no reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is guilty of the same offence` IF
    `is an officer or influential manager`
    AND (`consented, connived or conspired` OR `knowingly concerned` OR `knew or ought to have known and took no reasonable steps`)

§§ `19 -- composition`

-- s 19(1): an authorised officer may compound a prescribed compoundable offence "by collecting ... a sum not exceeding the
-- lower of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $5,000."
-- Which offences are prescribed is in regulations not retrieved. The base fine, not the continuing-offence add-on, is taken as
-- "the maximum fine that is prescribed" -- an INFERENCE.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the lower of` IS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum composition sum` IS
    `the lower of` (`the base fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

§§ `20, 22(5) -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 20(1): a person aggrieved may, "within 14 days after the date on which notice of the decision is served on the person,
-- appeal to the Minister" against "(a) the refusal to give written approval under section 10(1), 12(1) or 13(1); (b) an order
-- under section 10(2), 11(2) or 12(5); (c) the imposition of any condition of written approval under section 12(2) or 13(3)."
-- (2): the order "takes effect and must be complied with unless otherwise ordered by the Minister." (5): the decision is final.
-- Nothing else is appealable under s 20, including an information notice (s 15) or entry under s 9.
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `a refusal of approval for engineering works`
    `an upkeep order`
    `a condition on approval to lay infrastructure`
    `an information notice`
    `an entry on land`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is appealable` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `an information notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an entry on land` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `days after service` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `days after service` AT MOST 14

-- s 22(5): service takes effect "(c) if the document is sent by prepaid registered post, 2 days after the day the document was
-- posted (even if it is returned undelivered)". Personal delivery is taken as effective on the day it is given -- the section
-- does not say so; an INFERENCE. Days are day numbers; counting the 14 days from the day after service is an INFERENCE.
DECLARE Service IS ONE OF
    `personal delivery`
    `registered post`

GIVEN `the method` IS A Service, `day sent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the day service takes effect` IS
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `registered post` THEN `day sent` PLUS 2
    OTHERWISE `day sent`

GIVEN `how served` IS A Service, `day of sending` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the last day to appeal` IS
    `the day service takes effect` `how served` `day of sending` PLUS 14
